Read the Linux web view's pipe as UTF-8, in both directions.

JUCE's WebKitGTK backend runs the view in a forked child and talks to it over a
pipe of JSON commands. The writer encodes the JSON as UTF-8 (toRawUTF8), but the
reader rebuilt it with String (const char*, size_t), which takes each byte as
one 8-bit character. In the child, the string a script message handler hands
over (jsc_value_to_string, UTF-8) went through var (const char*), the same
8-bit reading. So every non-ASCII character was re-encoded as Latin-1 once per
crossing, and text that crossed repeatedly grew: a TONE3000 tone named
"EVH 5150III(R) 100S" came back from the page as "EVH 5150IIIÃ..Â(R)", and
every save and reload of the patch added more layers (issue #48).

Both now read UTF-8 (String::fromUTF8). ASCII is unchanged, and so are Windows
and macOS, which never use this pipe.

--- a/modules/juce_gui_extra/native/juce_WebBrowserComponent_linux.cpp
+++ b/modules/juce_gui_extra/native/juce_WebBrowserComponent_linux.cpp
@@ -683,7 +683,11 @@
         if (responder == nullptr)
             return;
 
-        const auto object = JSON::fromString (String (buffer.getData(), lengthsBuffer.getJsonLength()));
+        // PLECTRIFY_WEBKIT_UTF8_IPC: the JSON was written as UTF-8 (sendCommand
+        // uses toRawUTF8), so it must be read as UTF-8. String (const char*, n)
+        // reads bytes as 8-bit characters, which turned every non-ASCII
+        // character into mojibake once per crossing of the pipe.
+        const auto object = JSON::fromString (String::fromUTF8 (buffer.getData(), (int) lengthsBuffer.getJsonLength()));
 
         if (object.isVoid())
             return;
@@ -1014,7 +1018,8 @@
         auto& wk = *WebKitSymbols::getInstance();
 
         auto s = wk.juce_jsc_value_to_string (wk.juce_webkit_javascript_result_get_js_value (r));
-        CommandReceiver::sendCommand (outChannel, "invokeCallback", var (s));
+        // PLECTRIFY_WEBKIT_UTF8_IPC: jsc_value_to_string returns UTF-8.
+        CommandReceiver::sendCommand (outChannel, "invokeCallback", var (String::fromUTF8 (s)));
         wk.juce_g_free (s);
     }
 
